problems.problem:
Find all functions $f:\mathbb{C}\to\mathbb{R}^+$ that simultaneously satisfy the following conditions:

a) $f(uv)=f(u)f(v)$ for all $u,v\in\mathbb{C}$;

b) $f(\alpha u)=|\alpha|\,f(u)$ for all $\alpha\in\mathbb{R}$, $u\in\mathbb{C}$;

c) $f(u)+f(v)\le|u|+|v|$ for all $u,v\in\mathbb{C}$.

Determine all functions $f:\mathbb{R}_+\to\mathbb{R}_+$ such that:

a) $f(xf(y))f(y)=f(x+y)$ for $x,y\ge 0$;

b) $f(2)=0$;

c) $f(x)\ne 0$ for $0\le x<2$.

There are two piles of cards, one with $n$ cards and the other with $m$ cards. $A$ and $B$ play alternately, performing on each turn one of the following operations:

a) remove one card from one pile;

b) remove one card from each pile;

c) move one card from one pile to the other.

Player $A$ always starts the game, and whoever takes the last card wins. Determine, in terms of $m$ and $n$, whether there is a winning strategy, so that one of the players, following it, can always win.

There is a $2008\times 2008$ board with $2008$ counters, one in each row and each column of the board. It is allowed to perform one of the following moves:

a) two steps to the right and $10$ upwards;

b) two steps to the right and $6$ downwards;

c) two steps to the left and $6$ upwards;

d) two steps to the left and $10$ downwards.

If the path downwards cannot be completed, one jumps to the top of the same column and continues the path normally; analogously in the other directions. In each turn one counter is moved using any of the allowed operations. Is it possible that at some moment, after a finite number of turns, the counters are placed forming a square of side $44$ in the upper left corner of the board, and the remaining $72$ are in the last row in the first $72$ cells?
